mirror": lensFarReflection, and the TX lens branch reading the far face's light along it at the
transmitted roughness. It carries farFaceReflected with it (athenea f70c149's base, kFlagOwnFresnel's
splat half: the far face of a solid sends (1-R) R tint (1-R) of the light along its way back out
through the near face), which 0001's note left out: athenea's raster draws it, and without it a
clear ball reads 0.952 of the path traced one under a uniform sky. Only a solid glass (not a thin
wall, ior > 1, front-facing) changes.

